The issue was caused by the missing handling of `LO` and `LN` cases in the `readBinaryCustomData` function, which are responsible for reading latitude and longitude values. Without these cases, the buffer wasn't being properly consumed, leading to incorrect data being read as longitude and resulting in an `IllegalArgumentException`.

Here's the fixed function with the required cases added:

```java
    private void readBinaryCustomData(Position position, ByteBuf buf, String form) {
        CellTower cellTower = new CellTower();
        String[] keys = form.substring(1).split("%");
        for (String key : keys) {
            switch (key) {
                case "SA":
                    position.set(Position.KEY_SATELLITES, buf.readUnsignedByte());
                    break;
                case "MV":
                    position.set(Position.KEY_POWER, buf.readUnsignedShort() * 0.1);
                    break;
                case "BV":
                    position.set(Position.KEY_BATTERY, buf.readUnsignedShort() * 0.1);
                    break;
                case "GQ":
                    cellTower.setSignalStrength((int) buf.readUnsignedByte());
                    break;
                case "CE":
                    cellTower.setCellId(buf.readUnsignedInt());
                    break;
                case "LC":
                    cellTower.setLocationAreaCode(buf.readUnsignedShort());
                    break;
                case "CN":
                    int combinedMobileCodes = (int) (buf.readUnsignedInt() % 100000); // cccnn
                    cellTower.setMobileCountryCode(combinedMobileCodes / 100);
                    cellTower.setMobileNetworkCode(combinedMobileCodes % 100);
                    break;
                case "RL":
                    buf.readUnsignedByte(); // rxlev
                    break;
                case "PC":
                    position.set(Position.PREFIX_COUNT + 1, buf.readUnsignedInt());
                    break;
                case "AT":
                    position.setAltitude(buf.readUnsignedInt());
                    break;
