To fix this code, the main issue was that the function was incorrectly identifying the end of a frame by searching for the last occurrence of `']'` instead of the first. This caused the decoder to process multiple frames as a single frame. The solution involves modifying the loop to find the first occurrence of `']'`, ensuring each frame is processed individually.

### Fixed Code
```java
    @Override
    protected Object decode(
            ChannelHandlerContext ctx, Channel channel, ByteBuf buf) throws Exception {

        int endIndex = -1;
        for (int i = buf.readerIndex(); i < buf.writerIndex(); i++) {
            if (buf.getByte(i) == ']') {
                endIndex = i + 1;
                break;
            }
        }

        if (endIndex > 0) {
            ByteBuf frame = Unpooled.buffer();
            while (buf.readerIndex() < endIndex) {
                byte b1 = buf.readByte();
                if (b1 == '}') {
                    byte b2 = buf.readByte();
                    switch (b2) {
                        case 0x01:
