To fix this issue, the function needs to ensure that a trailing slash is appended after the port when it's present, regardless of whether the database name is provided or not.

Here is the fixed function:

```java
    @Override
    public String constructUrlFromEndpointPortDatabase(String endpoint, String port, String dbname) {
        String url = "jdbc:postgresql://" + endpoint;
        if (!StringUtils.isNullOrEmpty(port)) {
            url += ":" + port;
        }
        if (!StringUtils.isNullOrEmpty(port) || !StringUtils.isNullOrEmpty(dbname)) {
            url += "/";
        }
        if (!StringUtils.isNullOrEmpty(dbname)) {
            url += dbname;
        }
        return url;
    }
```

